    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 2e8b1cb2b0da45284ea57119600166d807474244 -->\n**Needs changes before merge: obsolete, main already carries this fix.**\n\nWhat looks good\n- The diff is exactly the one line described (`cutting: Vec::new()` in `thread_mill`, `crates/app/tests/coarse_rims.rs:134`), and it was the right repair for the build break at the time.\n\nLocal results (PR head trial-merged with current origin/main)\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test coarse_rims`: does not compile.\n```\nerror[E0062]: field `cutting` specified more than once\n   --> crates/app/tests/coarse_rims.rs:142   (first use at :134)\n```\n- Clippy not run (same compile error).\n\nCause: origin/main commit b5299968 \"test(app): coarse_rims sets the Tool cutting field\" already added `cutting: Vec::new()` at the end of the same literal. The merge is textually clean, so GitHub shows no conflict, but together the two lines declare the field twice and would re-break main's build.\n\nRequested before merge\n1. Do not merge this PR. Close it as a duplicate of b5299968 (issue #1349 is already fixed by that commit), or drop its one line.\n\nNotes (not blocking)\n- Other `Tool` literals on main were not audited further, since main's own build is the check once b5299968 is in.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
